      {
        "id": 546832189,
        "iid": 4088,
        "project_id": 34675721,
        "title": "fix(release): close the release notes directory handle",
        "description": "## Description\n\nRelease-note file lookup opens the repository directory with `os.OpenRoot` but never closes that handle.\nOn Windows, this prevents removal of the directory after the command returns.\nClose the directory on every return path and preserve file and directory close errors.\n\nCloses #8599\n\n## Validation\n\nThree regressions cover reading a file, falling back to text for a missing file, and a directory read error.\nEach case fails to remove its directory on the original Windows code and passes with this change.\nThe full release-create suite also passes, including the two existing cleanup failures reproduced in the issue.\nThe full affected package suite passes on Linux with Go 1.27.2.\n\n## AI assistance\n\nImplemented and tested with OpenAI Codex.",
